requirements:
Conserved seeds must be stored under dry, hermetic conditions using locally available and cost-effective resources:
a) Traditional containers such as earthen pots or bamboo baskets may be used if protective measures against moisture, pests, and rodents are provided;
b) Exposure to high humidity, heat, and direct sunlight must be strictly avoided;
c) For bulk storage, hermetically sealed moisture-impervious bins must NOT be used, as they cause heat and moisture accumulation in lower layers.
